-- =============================================================================
-- 0. THE NEW LINES, and the EMULATED camera reads kept on them — before A
-- moves the segments.  A read (corridor.vehicle_sightings) with source
-- 'emulated_anpr' attributed to a segment whose line changes keeps its place
-- ALONG that segment: ST_LineLocatePoint(old line, position) re-interpolated
-- on the new line.  Its segment, in this order:
--   1. the e-challan engine's attribution, the segment_id in its
--      recommendation's evidence (what an officer decides on)
--   2. the segment line the read already lies on (within 0.5 m — an
--      emulator read at a camera site on the network)
--   3. its camera's segment as registered BEFORE E re-sites the cameras
-- A read none of these attributes to a segment of this network stays where
-- it was recorded.  Only the position changes: ids, plate, time, speed,
